# .trivyignore — Known upstream CVEs in transitive dependencies
#
# These CVEs exist in transitive npm dependencies that are pulled in
# by the Node.js runtime or build tooling. They are not exploitable
# in our application context but trigger Trivy HIGH/CRITICAL findings
# that block deploys.
#
# Review this file periodically and remove entries once the upstream
# dependency ships a fix that flows into our lock file.
#
# To find blocking CVEs: run Trivy locally with --exit-code 1 and
# add verified CVE IDs here with documentation.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-03-04

# tar — DoS via deeply nested sub-folders during extraction.
# Mitigated by pnpm override to tar@7.5.10 in root package.json.
# Not exploitable: we do not extract untrusted tar archives at runtime.
CVE-2024-28863

# cross-spawn — ReDoS via crafted command string.
# Fixed in cross-spawn@7.0.5+; transitive dep from npm/npx internals.
# Not exploitable: we do not pass untrusted input to cross-spawn.
CVE-2024-21538
